  "caveats": [
    "No hardware isolation or cross-machine confidence interval; simultaneous system load can change timings.",
    "F32 probability-weight caching and BLAS tiling can change low bits. Independent dense-reference tests use 5-decimal tolerance; this is not upstream PyTorch or BF16 trained parity.",
    "Wide-option residual packing increases this witness workspace from 672256 to 828928 bytes; scratch remains bounded by a 32-option tile and linear in token count.",
    "The raw C ABI still scans caller-owned weights every run. Only the opaque copied-and-validated owner omits this repeated scan."
  ],
